course: dictionary
lesson: 6854
title: Oval, a shape and a sports field
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An oval is a shape with curves and no corners, like a squashed circle or an egg. «The shape of the follicle decides the shape of the hair: a round one grows straight hair, a flat or oval one grows curly hair.» Here oval describes the shape, so it must mean something like a stretched circle.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. The sentence compares oval with round and flat, which are also shapes, so the words around it tell you what kind of word oval is. Try swapping in "circle": it no longer fits, because an oval is not quite a circle.
explain: Oval can also name a place. In Australia, kids play sport on the school oval, which is a sports field, often oval-shaped, for cricket or football. Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it is about playing sport, oval means the field, not the shape.
fact: Oval means shaped like an egg or a stretched circle.
fact: In maths, an oval is a curved 2D shape with no corners. It is not a circle.
fact: «Oval» can also be a noun, meaning an oval shape, as in «an oval».
fact: In Australia, an oval is a sports field for cricket or football.
fact: «The Oval Office» is the name of the US president's office.
exercise: «Round follicles grow straight hair and flat or oval follicles grow curly hair.» What does oval describe here? | A type of curly hair | *A shape like a stretched circle | A sports field | A very round circle
exercise: In Australia, the kids ran out onto the school oval for cricket. What is the oval? | *A sports field | A pencil case | A shape drawn on paper | A bag for lunch
exercise: In maths, what makes an oval different from a circle? | It is always coloured red | It has three corners | *It is curved, has no corners, and is stretched rather than perfectly round | It has four straight sides
test: «Galaxies come in main shapes: spirals like ours, round or oval ellipticals, and shapeless irregulars.» What does oval mean here? | A shape with no shape at all | A bright star | A kind of spiral | *A stretched, egg-like shape
test: Which phrase uses oval to mean the US president's workplace? | Oval shape | *The Oval Office | The school oval | Oval-ball games
exam: «Artists start with light, simple shapes, circles, ovals and boxes, then add details on top.» What is an oval in this sentence? | A box with straight sides | A sports field | *A simple curved shape, like a stretched circle | A squashed circle, a curved shape with no corners
